\f0\fs32 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
What you will do for every new project:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Create a new empty local folder\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs34 \cf0 mkdir MyNewProject\
cd MyNewProject\
git init\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Copy the scaffold files from the bootstrap output into this new folder\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This means you copy the reusable files created by the first big prompt, for example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs34 \cf0 AI_PROJECT_BOOTSTRAP.md\
BOOTSTRAP_USAGE.md\
CLAUDE.md\
AGENTS.md\
GOVERNANCE.md\
CURRENT_STATE.md\
AI_HANDOFF.md\
ARTIFACT_REGISTRY.md\
TRACEABILITY_MATRIX.md\
SPECS/\
ADR/\
BACKLOG/\
REVIEWS/\
TESTS/\
WORKLOG/\
HANDOFFS/\
SCRIPTS/\
...\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf0 So now your new project folder contains the bootstrap system.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open Claude Code / Codex inside this new folder\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The AI must be working inside the new project folder, not inside the old bootstrap folder.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Paste the \'93new project initialization prompt\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
It tells the AI:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 read the bootstrap files\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 understand the governance system\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 inspect the new repo\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 take your new product idea\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 fill the scaffold with project-specific specs, architecture, backlog, ADRs, test plan, traceability, handoff, and current state\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 prepare the first implementation task\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 not start coding yet\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Paste your new project idea inside the prompt\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Inside this section:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs34 \cf0 Project input:\
\
[PASTE THE NEW PROJECT IDEA / PRD / FEATURE LIST / EXCEL SUMMARY / REQUIREMENTS HERE]\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf0 Replace that placeholder with your actual idea.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs34 \cf0 Project input:\
\
I want to build a contract lifecycle management SaaS for small legal teams.\
It should support contract intake, contract drafting, approval workflows,\
obligation tracking, renewal reminders, user roles, document storage,\
audit history, and dashboard reporting.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
